{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Whoever sheds the blood of man — in man.</b> The meaning is 'in man,' that is, in the presence of man, that is, in the presence of witnesses — his blood shall be shed by order of the court. And this is the intent of Targum Onkelos, who translated: דישוד דמא דאינשא בסהדין על מימר דיינא דמיה יתשד — 'who sheds the blood of man by testimony, by order of the judge his blood shall be shed.' Onkelos translated באדם as בסהדין — 'by witnesses.'" "<b>For in the image of Elohom He made</b> the one who made <b>man.</b> And by way of the Midrash: <b>And surely the blood of your lives will I require</b> — to include one who strangles himself. One might think even when unwilling; Scripture says, <b>'surely' (אך)</b>. One might think like Hananiah, Mishael, and Azariah; Scripture says, <b>'surely' (אך)</b>. <b>At the hand of every beast</b> — these are the four kingdoms, which were called beasts; <b>at the hand of man</b> — these are Israel, as it is said (Ezekiel 34): ״ואתן צאני צאן מרעיתי אדם אתם״; <b>at the hand of every man's brother</b> — these are the sons of Esau, as it is said (Genesis 32): ״הצילני נא מיד אחי מיד עשו״; <b>I will require the life of man</b> — in the time to come."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:11:25.516006699Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}